## Summary

This file is the server-side entry point that controls how your React Router application generates HTTP responses on the server.

This module should render the markup for the current page using a `<ServerRouter>` element with the `context` and `url` for the current request. This markup will (optionally) be re-hydrated once JavaScript loads in the browser using the client entry module.

This file is optional if you are running on Node. If it is not present, a default implementation will be used.
If you are using another runtime (i.e., Cloudflare) then you need to include this file. You can find sample implementations in the templates repository.

